    "items": [
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "How beautiful are your sandaled feet, princess! ,",
          "The curves of your thighs are like jewelry,",
          "the handiwork of a master."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Your navel is a rounded bowl;",
          "it never lacks mixed wine.",
          "Your belly is a mound of wheat",
          "surrounded by lilies."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Your breasts are like two fawns,",
          "twins of a gazelle."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Your neck is like a tower of ivory,",
          "your eyes like pools in Heshbon",
          "by Bath-rabbim’s gate.",
          "Your nose is like the tower of Lebanon",
          "looking toward Damascus."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Your head crowns you like Mount Carmel,",
          "the hair of your head like purple cloth —",
          "a king could be held captive in your tresses."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "How beautiful you are and how pleasant,",
          "my love, with such delights!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Your stature is like a palm tree;",
          "your breasts are clusters of fruit."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I said, “I will climb the palm tree",
          "and take hold of its fruit.”",
          "May your breasts be like clusters of grapes,",
          "and the fragrance of your breath like apricots."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Your mouth is like fine wine —"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Woman"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "flowing smoothly for my love,",
          "gliding past my lips and teeth!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I am my love’s,",
          "and his desire is for me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Come, my love,",
          "let’s go to the field;",
          "let’s spend the night among the henna blossoms."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let’s go early to the vineyards;",
          "let’s see if the vine has budded,",
          "if the blossom has opened,",
          "if the pomegranates are in bloom.",
          "There I will give you my caresses."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The mandrakes give off a fragrance,",
          "and at our doors is every delicacy,",
          "both new and old.",
          "I have treasured them up for you, my love."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
